# PR-EP-001 — Prior Discovery Validation

**Project:** BTA V5.1 — HCGO Enterprise Persistence Architecture

**Status:** LOCKED

**Classification:** Project Rule

**Version:** 1.0

---

# Purpose

Establish the methodology for incorporating previously approved architectural work into the current workstream while preventing both unnecessary rediscovery and architectural drift.

This Project Rule governs how prior Discoveries, Analyses, Architectural Decisions, Constitutional Guardrails, and other approved architectural artifacts are evaluated during the Enterprise Persistence Architecture effort.

---

# Project Rule

Previously approved architectural work shall **not** be automatically inherited.

Likewise, previously approved architectural work shall **not** be rediscovered.

Instead, every previously approved artifact shall undergo Prior Discovery Validation before becoming part of the current architectural baseline.

---

# Validation Process

Every inherited architectural artifact shall follow the same validation process.

```
Previously Approved Artifact
            │
            ▼
Retrieve Prior Determination
            │
            ▼
Review Against Current Scope
            │
            ▼
Identify New Discoveries
            │
            ▼
Determine Disposition
            │
            ▼
Approve Current Baseline
```

---

# Review Objectives

Each review shall:

- Preserve previously approved architectural work.
- Prevent unnecessary rediscovery.
- Identify newly discovered findings.
- Detect architectural drift.
- Maintain constitutional consistency.
- Maintain patent alignment.
- Produce a single authoritative architectural baseline.

---

# Disposition Classifications

Every reviewed artifact shall receive one of the following dispositions.

| Disposition | Definition |
|-------------|------------|
| **Confirmed** | Previous determination remains fully valid without modification. |
| **Expanded** | Previous determination remains valid with additional approved findings. |
| **Amended** | Previous determination requires approved modifications. |
| **Superseded** | Previous determination is replaced by a newly approved determination. |

---

# Review Criteria

Every inherited artifact shall be evaluated against:

- Current project scope
- Constitutional Guardrails
- Approved HCGO architecture
- Filed Patent (PPA)
- Newly approved discoveries
- Enterprise architecture objectives
- Future platform scalability

---

# Constitutional Constraint

No previously approved architectural determination shall be modified without explicit review and approval.

No previously approved determination shall be inherited without validation against the current workstream.

---

# Purpose Within Discovery

This Project Rule ensures Discovery becomes an iterative architectural refinement process rather than either:

- repeating previously completed work, or
- accepting prior work without validation.

The result is a continuously improving architectural baseline while preserving approved decisions and preventing architectural drift.

---

# Governance

This Project Rule applies to all:

- Discovery Findings
- Analysis Findings
- Constitutional Guardrails
- Architectural Decision Records (ADRs)
- Architecture Documents
- Enterprise Architecture artifacts

unless explicitly superseded by a future approved Project Rule.

